  "groundingSupports": [
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 128,
        "endIndex": 368,
        "text": "**What is confirmed:** Robotics AI startup Embo formally emerged from stealth announcing a $110M seed funding round led by Andreessen Horowitz (a16z), with participation from Khosla Ventures, DST Global, and Nvidia’s venture arm NVentures"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0,
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 370,
        "endIndex": 655,
        "text": "Founded by former Google DeepMind research scientists Danijar Hafner and Wilson Yan, Embo is building AI \"world models\" trained on internet video to serve as software brains for humanoid robots, enabling machines to simulate motor skills before executing tasks in physical environments"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0,
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 659,
        "endIndex": 805,
        "text": "**Important caveats:** Embo is pre-commercial and has not released a public product, third-party benchmark results, or customer deployment figures"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        2,
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 807,
        "endIndex": 901,
        "text": "Performance claims regarding out-of-the-box adaptability rely on simulated pre-training models"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        2,
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1076,
        "endIndex": 1271,
        "text": "**What is confirmed:** Google Research published a technical overview detailing DeepCrossAttention (DCA), an architectural revision to Transformer residual skip connections presented at ICML 2025"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        3,
        4
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1273,
        "endIndex": 1412,
        "text": "DCA replaces traditional point-wise residual addition with dynamic, per-token routing and depth-wise cross-attention across previous layers"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        3,
        5
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1414,
        "endIndex": 1566,
        "text": "Google reports DCA achieves equivalent model quality up to 3x faster in training time (or up to 5x fewer steps) while adding under 0.2% extra parameters"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        3,
        4
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1568,
        "endIndex": 1633,
        "text": "DCA can also be retrofitted onto existing pre-trained checkpoints"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        4,
        5
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1637,
        "endIndex": 1873,
        "text": "**Important caveats:** Performance gains and layer reduction figures (e.g., 29% depth reduction on LM1B) are drawn from Google's internal benchmarking on LM1B and C4 datasets, rather than independent evaluations on frontier-scale models"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        4
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1875,
        "endIndex": 1991,
        "text": "DCA increases memory-bandwidth overhead because intermediate representations from preceding layers must be preserved"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        5
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 2163,
        "endIndex": 2436,
        "text": "**What is confirmed:** Financial Times reporting by Martha Muir confirms power grid operators in North America and Europe are deploying Dynamic Line Rating (DLR) systems—combining field sensors and weather-aware software—to dynamically adjust transmission safety limits"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        6
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 2438,
        "endIndex": 2651,
        "text": "By calculating real-time conductor cooling from wind and ambient temperatures, operators are boosting existing transmission line capacity by 8% to 30% to accommodate surging electricity demand from AI data centers"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        6
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 2655,
        "endIndex": 2764,
        "text": "**Important caveats:** DLR optimizes existing transmission efficiency rather than generating new power supply"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        7
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 2766,
        "endIndex": 2867,
        "text": "Capacity gains fluctuate based on localized weather conditions and require ongoing sensor maintenance"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        7
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 3027,
        "endIndex": 3268,
        "text": "**What is confirmed:** *WIRED* published an interview with Michael Förtsch, CEO of Stuttgart-based startup Q.ANT, detailing data-center pilot tests of its Thin-Film Lithium Niobate (TFLN) photonic coprocessors hosted by cloud provider IONOS"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        8,
        9
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 3270,
        "endIndex": 3456,
        "text": "The processors use light waves rather than electrical signals to execute complex, non-linear calculations alongside standard GPUs and are manufactured using mature 90nm fabrication nodes"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        8,
        9
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 3460,
        "endIndex": 3623,
        "text": "**Important caveats:** The projected 4–5x energy reduction is based on theoretical simulations and has not been demonstrated on hardware in production benchmarks"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
